1. Permitted
   (a) Viewing the source code and using the built software for personal, non-commercial purposes.
   (b) Modifying and building the source code on your own machine for your personal use.

2. Prohibited (without prior written permission from the author)
   (a) Commercial use: use for profit or business, selling, or including it in paid or advertising-supported services.
   (b) Redistribution: providing, publishing, reposting or mirroring the source code, built files, any part of them,
       or modified versions of them to third parties (including re-uploading ZIP files, file sharing, or copying
       to other repositories).
   (c) Removing or altering this license notice.

3. GitHub
   While this repository is public, viewing and forking on GitHub are possible within the scope of the GitHub
   Terms of Service. Forking does not change the restrictions in section 2.

4. Third-party software
   Third-party software that is bundled or used (FFmpeg: LGPL, NAudio: MIT License, etc.) is covered by its own
   license. This license does not restrict the rights granted by those licenses.

5. No warranty
   This software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The author is not liable for any damages
   arising from its use.
